---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const structuredData = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Terms', item: `${SITE.url}/terms` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use | QuickOper"
  description="Terms of use for QuickOper. The calculators are informational estimates, not financial advice, and are provided without warranty."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <article class="text-ink-soft space-y-4">
    <h1 class="text-ink text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>

    <p class="text-ink-mute text-sm">Last updated {SITE.legalLastUpdated}.</p>

    <p>
      By using {SITE.name} you agree to these terms. They are short, and written to be read
      rather than skipped.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      This is information, not advice
    </h2>

    <p>
      The calculators produce <strong class="text-ink"
        >estimates for general information</strong
      >. Nothing on this site is financial, investment, tax, legal or accounting advice,
      and using it does not create a professional relationship of any kind.
    </p>

    <p>
      Nobody at {SITE.name} is a qualified financial adviser. We do not know your circumstances,
      and the calculators do not ask about them. For a decision that matters, speak to someone
      qualified who does.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      What the numbers are, and are not
    </h2>

    <p>
      We work hard to get the arithmetic right and publish exactly how it is checked on
      the{' '}
      <a class="text-brand underline" href="/methodology">methodology page</a>. Even so,
      every result rests on assumptions stated on the page that produced it. Real
      agreements involve daily interest, fees, promotional periods, variable rates and new
      spending that a calculator cannot know about.
    </p>

    <p>
      A result from this site is therefore <strong class="text-ink"
        >not a quote, an offer, or a statement of what any lender will actually charge you</strong
      >. Always check the figures against your own agreement and statements.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">No warranty</h2>

    <p>
      The site is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including as to accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose or
      uninterrupted availability.
    </p>

    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} and its author are not liable for
      any loss or damage arising from use of, or reliance on, this site — including financial
      loss resulting from a decision informed by a calculation here. Nothing in these terms
      excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Errors, and telling us about them
    </h2>

    <p>
      If you believe a figure is wrong, please{' '}
      <a class="text-brand underline" href="/contact">tell us</a>. We correct errors
      openly and record the change and its date on the affected page. Reporting one is
      welcome and is the most useful thing you can send us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Using the site and its content
    </h2>

    <p>
      You may use the calculators freely, for personal or commercial purposes. Please do
      not:
    </p>

    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>republish the written explanations as your own;</li>
      <li>present results from this site as professional financial advice;</li>
      <li>attempt to disrupt the site or the people using it.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The written content and design are the author's. The source code is public at{' '}
      <a class="text-brand underline" href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener">GitHub</a> so the arithmetic
      can be inspected and verified; publishing it there is not a grant of a licence to redistribute
      it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Linking to any page here is welcome and needs no permission. If you would like to
      embed a calculator, <a class="text-brand underline" href="/contact">get in touch</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Advertising and links to other sites
    </h2>

    <p>
      The site may carry advertising, or links to products or services where we would be
      paid a commission. Any such link will be labelled where it appears. We are not
      responsible for the content, products or privacy practices of any site we link to,
      and a link is not an endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes</h2>

    <p>
      These terms may change. The date at the top shows when they last did, and continuing
      to use the site after a change means you accept it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>

    <p>
      <a class="text-brand underline" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
